'''Shulkunaak''' is a red Dragon who can be found in a cave complex, he will give you information regarding the Sorcerer-king [[Blades:Celemaril|Celemaril]]. He is encountered during the quest [[Blades:Facing the Dragon|Facing the Dragon]].
{{NewLeft}}

==Related Quests==
*{{Quest Link|Facing the Dragon}}

==Quest-Related Events==
:''"Who dares disturb my peace? Speak, volaan. Your life hangs in the balance."''
::'''I am <Player Name>, and I seek your wisdom.'''
::''"You came here alone? That was very brave, or very stupid."''

:::'''I'm not afraid of you.'''
:::''"Stupidity it is, then. If it is death you seek, I will give it to you."''

:::'''I trust your good judgment with my life.'''
:::''"Ahkrin - bravery - may impress your peers. All it will earn you here is a quick death."''

::'''I am <Player Name>, and I don't fear you!'''
::''"Do you think it wise to provoke me, here in my own lair?"''
:::'''I see no other option for a coward like you.'''
:::''"Do not think you can provoke me that easily. But I admire your bravado."''

:::'''I am told dragons appreciate confidence.'''
:::''"Your ahkrin - bravery - has earned my respect. But that will not save your life."''

Both will lead to:
:''"But first, tell me. Why did you come all the way here to die?"''
:'''The Sorcerer-king Celemaril has returned.'''

You can choose to continue talking to Shulkunaak to gain the information, or begin a fight for it.

{|cellpadding="10" cellspacing="10" width="100%"
|-
! Talk to Shulkunaak
|-
|style="border: dotted 1px black;"|

:''"So the rumors are true. Krosis sul! I hoped this day would never come. You seek my help, then."''

:'''You're the only one who can help.'''

:''"Very well. Celemaril must not achieve his goals. The world cannot be destroyed just yet.<br>Know this: the Sorcerer-King is immortal. Simply destroying his physical form will not kill him."''

:'''So, he cannot be defeated?'''

:''"You need to bind his spirit first. But that will not be easy to accomplish."''

:'''What do we need?'''

:''"Have you already found the [[BL:Elder Scroll|Elder Scroll]]?"''

:'''We have.'''

:''"The Kel, the Elder Scroll, can affect all possible futures. you must bind the Sorcerer-King to the one where he fails to escape.<br>You will also need the incantation that was used to bind his spirit in ancient times.<br>Defeat Celemaril in combat. A pure heart must read the incantation while wearing his lost crown.<br>Celemaril's ancient crown is another matter. I do not know where it may now be found."''

:'''That's it?'''

:''"Yes. That should not be too hard for you, kendov."''

:'''Thank you for your help, great Shulkunaak.'''

:''"Do not thank me yet. Now you must prove yourself worthy to face the Sorcerer-King."''

:'''It doesn't have to be this way.'''

:''"There is no evading your duty, Blade."''

:'''Me, a Blade?!'''/'''Is it that obvious?'''

:''"Zu'u ni mey. I did not survive this long without knowing a Blade when I see one.<br>Have the Blades forgotten their sworn duty as dragonslayers? I assure you, I have not."''

::'''I don't care, this is unfair.'''

:::''"Fairness is irrelevant. Either you are a <man/woman> of honor, and you fight.<br>Or you are not honorable, and I kill you.<br>Now honor your comrades, and fight me! Aav grah!"''

::::'''Very well.'''

:::::''"I knew you were a <man/woman> of honor. Aav grah!"''


::'''Not if I kill you first.'''

:::''"Aav grah! Let us test ourselves against each other, <Player Name>!"''

Once enough damage has been dealt to Shulkunaak the following dialogue will begin:

:''"Enough. You have proven your worth.<br>Drem wah hi. Go in peace, Blade."''

:'''You have my gratitude, and that of my town.'''

:''"None of that will matter until you use it to stop Celemaril. Kfir voth ahkrin."''
|}
 
{|cellpadding="10" cellspacing="10" width="100%"
|-
! Fight Shulkunaak
|-
|style="border: dotted 1px black;"|
:''"So the rumors are true. Krosis sul! I hoped this day would never come. You seek my help, then."''

:'''Yes, and you'll tell me, or else!'''

:''"You choose death, then. Ol hi hind. So be it."''

Once enough damage has been dealt to Shulkunaak the following dialogue will begin:

:''"You have defeated me. I am gronsezin - honor-bound - to tell you what you need to know."''

:'''Tell me what we need to defeat the Sorcerer-king.'''

:''"I will tell you what you need to know.<br>Know this: the Sorcerer-King is immortal. Simply destroying his physical form will not kill him."''

:'''So, he cannot be defeated?'''

:''"You need to bind his spirit first. But that will not be easy to accomplish."''

:'''What do we need?'''

:''"Have you already found the Elder Scroll?"''

:'''We have.'''

:''"The Kel, the Elder Scroll, can affect all possible futures. you must bind the Sorcerer-King to the one where he fails to escape.<br>You will also need the incantation that was used to bind his spirit in ancient times.<br>Defeat Celemaril in combat. A pure heart must read the incantation while wearing his lost crown.<br>Celemaril's ancient crown is another matter. I do not know where it may now be found."''

:'''That's it?'''

:''"I have told you everything I know. The rest is up to you."''
|}
==Notes==
*Shulkunaak was originally orange, but was changed to maroon in a later patch.
* ''Shulkunaak'' may translate to "Sun-Moonlight-Eat" (Shul-Kun-Naak) or "Sun-Moonlight-Guide" (Shul-Kun-Aak) in  the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon Language]].


